1
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:05,674
1930年，经济学家凯恩斯写下一个预言：
In 1930, the economist John Maynard Keynes made a prediction:

2
00:00:05,774 --> 00:00:11,890
百年之后，机器将承担大部分工作，人们每周只需工作十五小时。
a century on, machines would do most of the work, and people would need to work just fifteen hours a week.

3
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:15,193
一百年快到了，机器越来越能干，
The century is nearly up, and machines have indeed grown ever more capable,

4
00:00:15,293 --> 00:00:17,641
我们却并没有因此变得轻松。
yet we are no more at ease.

5
00:00:17,681 --> 00:00:22,992
当机器能生产一切，明天属于谁？
When machines can produce everything, whose tomorrow will it be?

6
00:00:27,842 --> 00:00:33,321
回望七万年，人类的每一次飞跃，都伴随着劳动方式的巨变。
Looking back over seventy thousand years, every leap humankind made came with a great change in the way we work.

7
00:00:33,421 --> 00:00:38,447
认知革命，让智人学会用故事组织大规模的协作。
The Cognitive Revolution taught Sapiens to organise hundreds, even thousands, through shared stories.

8
00:00:38,547 --> 00:00:41,158
农业革命带来了剩余的粮食，
The Agricultural Revolution brought surplus grain,

9
00:00:41,258 --> 00:00:45,523
也带来了粮仓、私有财产、阶级和国家。
and with it granaries, private property, classes and the state.

10
00:00:45,623 --> 00:00:48,324
工业革命用蒸汽取代了肌肉，
The Industrial Revolution replaced muscle with steam,

11
00:00:48,424 --> 00:00:52,412
也把千百万农民变成了工厂里的雇佣工人。
and turned millions of peasants into wage workers in factories.

12
00:00:52,452 --> 00:01:00,540
手推磨产生的是封建主的社会，蒸汽磨产生的是工业资本家的社会。
The hand-mill gives you society with the feudal lord; the steam-mill, society with the industrial capitalist.

13
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:04,853
生产力变了，生产关系迟早也要跟着改变。
When the forces of production change, the relations of production must sooner or later follow.

14
00:01:04,953 --> 00:01:09,591
赫拉利说，人类靠共同相信的故事团结在一起；
Harari says humans are bound together by the stories they share;

15
00:01:09,691 --> 00:01:15,414
历史唯物主义还要追问：故事的背后，是谁在劳动，谁在占有？
historical materialism asks further: behind the stories, who does the work, and who owns the wealth?

16
00:01:17,814 --> 00:01:21,476
今天，一台新的“蒸汽机”正在轰鸣。
Today, a new "steam engine" is roaring to life.

17
00:01:21,576 --> 00:01:26,743
人工智能像电力一样，是一种通用技术，会渗入每个行业。
Like electricity, AI is a general-purpose technology; it will seep into every industry.

18
00:01:26,843 --> 00:01:31,584
这一次，最先被冲击的不是工厂，而是写字楼。
This time, the first to be hit is not the factory, but the office tower.

19
00:01:31,684 --> 00:01:36,269
过去的机器替代双手，人还能转向用头脑的工作；
The machines of the past replaced our hands, and people could still turn to work of the mind;

20
00:01:36,369 --> 00:01:41,380
这一次，人工智能替代头脑，具身智能替代双手。
this time, AI replaces the mind, and embodied AI replaces the hands.

21
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:47,640
无人工厂、无人农场、无人办公室——大部分岗位都将被取代。
Unmanned factories, unmanned farms, unmanned offices: most jobs will be replaced.

22
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:55,205
《未来简史》担心，21世纪会出现一个庞大的“无用阶级”。
Homo Deus fears the twenty-first century may create a vast "useless class".

23
00:01:55,305 --> 00:01:59,726
可“无用”的根源不在技术，而在资本主义的生产关系：
Yet the root of "uselessness" lies not in technology, but in capitalist relations of production:

24
00:01:59,826 --> 00:02:04,213
不占有生产资料的人，只能靠出卖劳动力为生；
those who own no means of production can live only by selling their labour power;

25
00:02:04,313 --> 00:02:09,446
生产领域一旦不再需要他们的劳动，他们就成了“无用”的人。
once production no longer needs their labour, they become "useless".

26
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:13,353
于是财富堆积如山，多数人却没了收入——
So wealth piles up like mountains, while most people lose their income —

27
00:02:13,653 --> 00:02:16,817
机器造出的商品，又卖给谁？
and who, then, will buy what the machines produce?

28
00:02:16,917 --> 00:02:21,305
问题，从“还有没有工作”，变成了“财富如何分配”。
The question shifts from "Will there be work?" to "How will the wealth be shared?"

29
00:02:21,505 --> 00:02:24,018
这正是历史唯物主义揭示的矛盾：
This is the contradiction historical materialism reveals:

30
00:02:24,318 --> 00:02:28,706
生产力一路飞奔，生产关系却原地踏步。
the forces of production race ahead, while the relations of production stand still.

31
00:02:29,006 --> 00:02:32,893
有人想踩刹车，可历史的刹车从来踩不住：
Some want to slam on the brakes, but history's brakes have never held:

32
00:02:32,993 --> 00:02:36,643
卢德派砸毁了织布机，机器却越来越多；
the Luddites smashed the looms, yet the machines only multiplied;

33
00:02:36,743 --> 00:02:41,037
明清海禁锁住了港口，换来的却是落后挨打。
the Ming and Qing sea bans locked the ports, and bought only backwardness and defeat.

34
00:02:41,137 --> 00:02:42,626
技术的洪流挡不住；
The flood of technology cannot be held back;

35
00:02:42,926 --> 00:02:47,848
我们能决定的，是修建怎样的堤坝，让水流向哪里。
what we can decide is what kind of dykes to build, and where the water will flow.

36
00:02:50,248 --> 00:02:53,583
摆在我们面前的，是三种明天。
Before us lie three tomorrows.

37
00:02:53,683 --> 00:02:57,356
第一种：征税、发补贴，修修补补。
In the first, tax and subsidy patch things up.

38
00:02:57,656 --> 00:03:02,983
可税高了资本不干，税低了，补贴少，市场撑不住。
But tax too high and capital balks; too low, subsidies shrink and the market cannot hold.

39
00:03:03,083 --> 00:03:07,322
第二种：算力和数据，集中在少数人手中。
In the second, computing power and data are concentrated in a few hands.

40
00:03:07,422 --> 00:03:12,417
《今日简史》早就警告过：谁拥有数据，谁就拥有未来。
21 Lessons warned long ago: whoever owns the data owns the future.

41
00:03:12,517 --> 00:03:18,353
少数人成了云端的领主，其余的人得到的是施舍，而不是权利。
A few become lords of the cloud; everyone else receives charity, not rights.

42
00:03:18,753 --> 00:03:24,537
第三种：生产资料归全社会所有，人人都是机器的共同主人。
In the third, the means of production belong to all of society, and everyone is a co-owner of the machines.

43
00:03:24,637 --> 00:03:27,910
借助人工智能和大数据，有计划地生产——
With AI and big data, production is planned —

44
00:03:28,210 --> 00:03:31,259
为了人的需要，而不是为了利润。
for human need, not for profit.

45
00:03:31,299 --> 00:03:36,889
基本需要，按需分配；稀缺资源，按贡献分配。
Basic needs, according to need; scarce resources, according to contribution.

46
00:03:36,929 --> 00:03:42,568
劳动不再只是谋生的手段，人们可以去创造、学习、照顾彼此。
Work is no longer merely a means of survival; people are free to create, to learn, and to care for one another.

47
00:03:42,608 --> 00:03:50,633
每个人的自由发展，是一切人的自由发展的条件。
The free development of each is the condition for the free development of all.

48
00:03:51,283 --> 00:03:54,517
但这样的明天，不会自动到来。
But such a tomorrow will not arrive on its own.

49
00:03:54,617 --> 00:03:59,153
八小时工作制，是工人们一次次走上街头争取来的；
The eight-hour day was won by workers taking to the streets, again and again;

50
00:03:59,193 --> 00:04:03,022
技术决定可能性，制度决定结果。
Technology decides what is possible; institutions decide what happens.

51
00:04:03,062 --> 00:04:06,807
而制度，由人选择，靠人争取。
And institutions are chosen by people, and won by people.

52
00:04:06,907 --> 00:04:10,498
马克思说：人们自己创造自己的历史。
As Marx wrote, people make their own history.

53
00:04:10,848 --> 00:04:13,417
明天属于谁？
So, whose tomorrow is it?

54
00:04:13,517 --> 00:04:17,895
属于每一个为它共同奋斗的人。
It belongs to everyone who strives for it, together.

